WEBVTT

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:05.800
Everyone, when you're watching Deltora Quest,

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:09.100
make sure you're in a well-lit
room and sit far away from the TV!

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:24.040
If I open this door, I'll find a new world

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:28.460
A world only just beginning

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:34.720
Even if there are tough times ahead

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:41.100
I'm sure I'll make it through

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:48.520
Now I'm making my way through this new world

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:54.860
And I've got hopes and dreams

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:57.700
I'm excited, I'm restless

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:01.200
Nobody can stop me

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:01.240
My heart is all fired up
Nobody can stop me

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:06.370
My heart is all fired up

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:10.420
From here I'll leap into the world

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:10.460
Taking to the sky
From here I'll leap into the world

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.590
Taking to the sky

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:19.680
Aiming for tomorrow and beyond

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:26.060
I believe that someday I'll grow up

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:31.070
That's why I'll spread my wings wide

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:54.800
The Japanese Deltora Quest is brought to you in English by ToranSubs

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:56.950
<i>My name is Lief.</i>

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.250
<i>And I'm Jasmine.</i>

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:03.420
<i>We're currently travelling to seven perilous places in order to recover the seven stolen gems!</i>

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:07.430
<i>We've already acquired the topaz,
ruby, opal, and the lapis lazuli!</i>

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:10.940
<i>We had to face some monsters, but they weren't anything we couldn't handle!</i>

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:16.940
<i>Hey now, we don't know what kinds of enemies we'll have to face in the future. You both need to be careful.</i>

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:19.540
<i>Geez, you worry too much, Barda!</i>

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.250
<i>And right now, we're headed to
Dread Mountain where the fifth gem is located!</i>

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:36.400
"Who am I? All is darkness but I will not despair.

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:38.920
Three things I know:

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:40.600
I know I am a man.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:42.650
I know where I have been.

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:45.000
I know what I must do.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.630
For now, that is enough."

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:52.120
That's so creepy... Just who in the
world wrote that? And why?

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:56.810
Well, he was living in this dark
cave without anyone to talk to.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:01.350
He likely wrote that for the sake
of maintaining his own sanity.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.920
I wonder what happened
to him afterwards...

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:05.800
Take a good look at his writing.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.700
It has darkened, probably with age.

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:15.600
Therefore, it's likely that he wrote this in his own blood while wounded. Whether he survived or not, I can't say.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:22.100
With the line "I know where I have been", could it be that he came from the Shadowlands?

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:27.620
I'd doubt that. Not one person has ever
succeeded in escaping the Shadowlands.

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:30.500
Then, what did he mean by that?

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:38.800
Just forget about that and go to sleep. All we need to focus on right now is resting our bodies and healing our wounds.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:44.860
Otherwise, we may very well meet the same fate in the future as the man who wrote that message.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.690
You guys should sleep as well. Goodnight.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:51.000
Looks like your injuries are all better now!

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:55.320
I wasn't expecting the green
moss to be this effective!

00:04:55.320 --> 00:05:01.910
Yeah, but if our injuries have healed in this time, the same should be the case for the Vraal.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:05.350
It may attack us again if
we stay here any longer.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:11.190
I wouldn't worry about that. That monster seems to think of nothing except fighting.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:17.470
I doubt that it's smart enough to use the green moss to heal its wounds.

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:21.520
That's right! There's no way that monster knows about the green moss!

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:28.550
Only those who have lived here for a long time like the Kin and the Dread Gnomes know about the moss, that's what Mama-

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:31.640
That's what Mama said...

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:38.400
Your mother and the other Kin must be worried sick about you by now, Prin...

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:45.190
I'm sure they already know that I'm safe here. They would have visited us in their dreams last night, after all...

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:48.560
Oh, that's right. They have the water
from the Dreaming Spring...!

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:53.600
Yeah. Mama and the others might
even be with us here right now...

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:57.950
And if they are here, I want
to apologise to them...

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:03.620
I'm sorry for making you all worry, but I will come back safely! I promise!

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:08.530
Don't worry. We'll definitely
protect Prin, no matter what.

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:12.500
That's right. So you can be at ease, everyone.

00:06:43.640 --> 00:06:45.100
I see...

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:48.460
It seems that they actually
defeated the Vraal...

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:49.800
Shall we resume our pursuit?

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:52.600
No, that won't be necessary.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:58.100
They'll be meeting something far more frightening than the Vraal at the top of Dread Mountain, anyway.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:00.910
They are certain to meet their end there.

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:12.000
So this is the Boolong forest, our old home! Now I can visit it in my dreams like the others, too!

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:15.830
Lief, hurry up! This way, this way!

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:22.050
She really is a Kin, child or otherwise...

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.260
They have such strong hides...!

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:26.100
I'm still getting cuts, though...

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:30.730
Well, at this pace, I'd say we'll reach the top of the mountain by the end of the day.

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:34.220
Yeah, and that's where
the fifth gem is hidden.

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:40.080
Wait, what are you guys standing
around for? Hurry up, hurry up!

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:43.800
I've found so many Boolong
cones lying around here!

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:45.440
Time to eat!

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:49.650
You sure seem to be having fun, Prin.

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:51.300
Of course I am!

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:54.600
I've always wanted to visit this place!

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:55.430
Here.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:59.820
At any rate, do the Boolong
thorns really not hurt you at all?

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:02.250
Not even a little!

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:05.190
Ah! I can see more tasty cones!

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:09.950
That's...

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:13.010
That should be enough for now, Prin.

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:16.360
What's wrong, Prin?

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:17.500
I found something!

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:24.000
What have you found?

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:31.520
A hut...?

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:33.750
Who on earth would live out here?

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:36.430
It's a gnome-rest! I'm sure of it!

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:37.800
So that mark is...

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:39.390
It belongs to the Dread Gnomes!

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:41.610
It seems to have been abandoned, though...

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:48.300
No one's here.

00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:03.110
It sure is a small space...

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:05.520
That's because the Dread
Gnomes are also small.

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:09.200
It feels a little strange.
It's as if we've become giants.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:13.990
According to Mama, there were gnome-rests all over the place in the past.

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:18.600
And they were all connected
by roads like a spider's web!

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:25.680
And after the Kin left, the Boolong trees increased in number to the point where they couldn't use these huts anymore, then...

00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:29.720
But... I wonder if that's really the only
reason why they abandoned them...

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:31.040
What do you mean?

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:36.500
Well, think about it. They chose to abandon all of these huts that they painstakingly built...

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:39.300
There must be a pretty
serious reason for that.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:40.710
You have a point...

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:46.580
Something definitely happened here. Something we have no way of knowing about must have changed.

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:47.880
I see...

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:50.400
I can hear something...!

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:51.570
Someone's coming...!

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:53.190
Is it the Dread Gnomes...?

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:58.310
This is bad. We won't have anywhere to escape if they enter this hut...!

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:01.400
Don't come this way, please...!

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:12.480
It would seem that there's a Dread Gnome road nearby. Let's have a look.

00:10:13.490 --> 00:10:15.310
I think it's in this direction.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:20.000
Stay vigilant. They might still be around.

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:25.000
There really is one here...!

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:31.660
I was careless...! Even though the entire
mountain is covered with Boolong trees,

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:36.150
it would still make sense for them to secure one or two roads for means of contacting one another...

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:38.420
Had we found this sooner-

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:41.910
What are these? They look
similar to Boolong cones, but...

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:43.070
It's a blister!

00:10:43.070 --> 00:10:45.000
But what is it doing out here?

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:47.500
Perfect! This will come in handy!

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:50.710
I wonder if the Dread Gnomes
from earlier dropped this...

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:55.000
There is a road leading to the
Shadowlands at the base of the mountain.

00:10:55.310 --> 00:11:01.840
So, it wouldn't surprise me if the Dread Gnomes have been scheming with the Shadowlands in some way.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:07.910
That can't be true. Mama said that the Dread Gnomes hate the Shadow Lord, after all!

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:11.700
They even make traps
to hurt the Grey Guards!

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:15.250
In the past that may have been true, but who knows if that's still the case?

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:17.300
It's definitely still the same now!

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:20.020
Anyway, let's just keep moving for now.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:20.820
Yeah.

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:41.240
A dead end...?

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:44.140
Then where did those Dread
Gnomes disappear to...?

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:47.510
Be careful. There may be traps here. Let's go.

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:48.890
Kree!

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:56.210
It's a door!

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:05.150
W-Wait a second! Are you really
planning on going inside...?!

00:12:05.150 --> 00:12:07.830
This is the Dread Gnomes' hideout, you know?!

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:10.720
Even so, we have no choice but to go.

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:13.700
There's something we must find, after all.

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:16.660
And there's a high chance that
it's in the Dread Gnomes' hands.

00:12:16.660 --> 00:12:18.220
That's exactly right...!

00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:24.890
No good; it won't move an inch.

00:12:25.290 --> 00:12:27.100
I wonder what these marks mean...

00:12:27.450 --> 00:12:29.000
They seem to be words, but...

00:12:30.460 --> 00:12:31.900
I can't really make them out...

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:34.200
Aren't they just random marks?

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:40.100
I see! I get it now!

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:10.150
Look, if you smear it with
the white sand like this...

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:14.640
"Find an arrow, straight and narrow.

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:16.550
This will be your front door key.

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:20.070
Find its mate upon the gate.
Turn it full. Push, don't pull."

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:21.880
Is it supposed to be a riddle...?

00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:24.390
It comes across as a bit childish, though...

00:13:30.260 --> 00:13:31.010
It fits!

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:37.360
That really is very simple. If an arrow is the answer, then they shouldn't just leave it lying on the floor by the door.

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:40.480
Perhaps the Dread Gnomes
just aren't very bright?

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:47.880
The Dread Gnomes are very cunning. Mama also said that they love tricks and traps.

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:49.670
So we really need to be more careful...

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:52.210
I understand. It's alright, Prin.

00:13:58.500 --> 00:13:59.500
I see...

00:13:59.800 --> 00:14:02.000
So this is the Dread Gnome's stronghold...

00:14:02.390 --> 00:14:04.600
I wonder how far this passage goes...

00:14:07.020 --> 00:14:09.530
You guys heard laughter just now, right?

00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:12.520
You don't think it was just some birds?

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:16.950
No, that was definitely
a person laughing...!

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:21.720
It must be the Dread Gnomes! They're laughing at us because we fell for their trap!

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:27.480
It doesn't matter who it is, I'll make sure that they regret laughing at us! Let's go!

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:28.160
Yeah.

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:29.500
You can't!

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:34.100
I'm sorry, Lief... Are you okay...?

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:36.450
Y-Yeah, I'm alri-

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:44.000
Guys, come back! It really is a trap!

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:48.560
Jasmine!

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:03.580
Don't look down!

00:15:03.580 --> 00:15:03.870
-Pull me up, quick!!
Don't look down!

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:04.900
Let's get out of here!
-Pull me up, quick!!

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:05.320
-Hurry!!
Let's get out of here!

00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:06.000
-Hurry!!

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:11.400
Tell me, Lief. How did
you know that it was a trap?

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:13.000
The marks on the door.

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:17.500
As it turns out, it wasn't just
some random mark or scratches...

00:15:18.190 --> 00:15:19.380
It was a hidden code.

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:21.820
"If you wish to die..."

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:27.200
"Find its mate upon the gate. Turn it full. Push, don't pull. If you wish to die..."

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:29.910
So... should we try pulling it, then?

00:15:30.100 --> 00:15:31.000
Yeah.

00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:33.710
Let's try it one more time.

00:15:39.010 --> 00:15:40.750
Good, looks like we're in the clear.

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:42.720
Wait, let's see.

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:50.840
It seems to be safe.

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:55.500
Be careful, I'm sure that there
are still a lot of traps around.

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:58.080
Yeah. Watch your step, everyone.

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:07.420
Is it just me, or is this passage
getting smaller and smaller?

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:12.100
This will become difficult if
it gets any smaller than this...

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:16.900
Which path should we take?

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:18.700
The middle one, of course.

00:16:19.760 --> 00:16:21.630
It's the largest of them all.

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:23.740
<i>That's</i> your reasoning?

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:28.920
And it's perfectly good reasoning. It's probably going to be dangerous no matter which route we choose.

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:32.400
Therefore, why not pick the
middle one as Barda says?

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:47.640
It's them!

00:16:47.640 --> 00:16:51.780
Hear me! We have no
intention of fighting you!

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:55.500
Drop your weapons! Once you
do, we will do the same!

00:16:56.020 --> 00:16:57.600
Don't give them any opportunities.

00:16:57.960 --> 00:17:02.670
Why didn't you answer us?! We've made it clear that we don't want to fight you guys!

00:17:02.940 --> 00:17:04.240
What a load of crap!

00:17:04.760 --> 00:17:07.270
Do you really think we
can trust your words?!

00:17:07.270 --> 00:17:10.260
We trust only the words of
the great Gellick and no one else!!

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:12.590
Stop this! There is no reason for us to fight!

00:17:16.570 --> 00:17:18.800
We will fight for the great Gellick!

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:21.300
This is getting us nowhere...!

00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:23.280
Let's run!

00:17:38.770 --> 00:17:40.000
Hurry, Barda!

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:05.420
Oh no...!

00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:12.610
They got us...!

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:14.500
Darn...!

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:20.060
It's getting hard to breathe in here...

00:18:20.060 --> 00:18:22.520
There's barely enough air in this place...

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:25.790
Seems like it's a perfectly sealed room...

00:18:25.990 --> 00:18:31.760
No way...! Then we will run out of air until we can't breathe anymore?

00:18:31.760 --> 00:18:33.740
Are we going to die here?

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:37.420
Calm down, Prin. It's going to be okay.

00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:43.700
The Dread Gnomes are sure to come again, if only to laugh at our suffering faces.

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:46.000
And that will be our chance to escape.

00:18:46.590 --> 00:18:48.950
You're right. They will definitely come.

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:53.440
Otherwise, it would make no sense to go to the trouble of trapping us in here.

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:57.220
They can kill us at any time with
their poisoned arrows, after all.

00:18:57.540 --> 00:19:01.140
But the problem is, we don't
know when they will come again...

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:02.740
If only we knew that...

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:05.160
I'm so thirsty...

00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:09.600
If it's water that you need, I still have some from the Dreaming Spring, if that's good enough.

00:19:10.780 --> 00:19:13.120
Wait, that's a thought! Why not just dream?

00:19:13.640 --> 00:19:19.630
If we drink the water from the Dreaming Spring, we can see what they're planning in our dreams!

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:23.200
That way, we'll surely figure
out a means of escape!

00:19:41.870 --> 00:19:43.300
Relax, Lief.

00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:46.200
There's nothing to fear.

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:50.460
This is just a dream. We do
not exist to these people.

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:51.600
Yeah.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:52.900
I know.

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:54.600
Let's go.

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:17.400
Watch what you're doing! You'll die if you get even a drop of that on you!

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:18.840
S-Sorry...

00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:22.240
Is this poison...?

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:26.550
I see! So this is the poison that the
Dread Gnomes use on their arrows!

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:49.530
<i>That's</i> 'Gellick'...?!

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:54.920
More...! Bring more to me!

00:20:55.120 --> 00:20:59.750
Please forgive us, great Gellick! In truth, that was the last of our supply for today!

00:21:00.960 --> 00:21:04.400
What was that? There's no more...?!

00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:08.220
Please forgive us, but we can only
breed so many grubs at one time...

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:16.850
What a cruel beast!

00:21:17.120 --> 00:21:20.120
He's killing his subordinates
just to demonstrate his strength...!

00:21:20.430 --> 00:21:21.700
Even though...

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:25.600
...we too were once a proud tribe...

00:21:26.120 --> 00:21:30.580
Even though all of these
riches were once ours...!

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:37.340
What's the matter? What are you mumbling
about over there, Gla-Thon?

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:40.520
N-Nothing, great Gellick!
Gla-Thon meant nothing by it...!

00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:45.120
Is that true? Are you sure she doesn't
have some kind of problem with me...?

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:51.800
M-Most certainly not! We would never have any complaints about you, great Gellick!

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:58.190
I see... It would seem that the Dread Gnomes are
completely under that monster's control...

00:21:58.190 --> 00:21:59.400
Very well, then!

00:21:59.800 --> 00:22:05.000
If you all wish to not be turned to
stone, then bring me more food!

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:10.420
If you don't have any grubs left here, then go and catch some outside around the mountain!

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:14.300
Foolish humans...

00:22:20.090 --> 00:22:21.000
Over there...!

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:23.400
It's the emerald, the symbol of honour...!

00:22:24.150 --> 00:22:28.010
The fifth gem of the Belt of Deltora...!

00:22:38.580 --> 00:22:47.800
How long has it truly been, I wonder?

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:57.680
I've been watching the moon all this time, bathing in its light

00:22:57.680 --> 00:23:05.150
As we moved closer, a goddess passed over us

00:23:05.150 --> 00:23:14.870
And just like that, my little dream was carried away

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:20.460
I saw you when I looked to the night sky

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:20.500
Now that I think of it, your name was written there too
I saw you when I looked to the night sky

00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:25.090
Now that I think of it, your name was written there too

00:23:25.790 --> 00:23:29.380
Above me, a shooting star

00:23:29.380 --> 00:23:32.800
fades into the distance

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:38.470
When the moonlight starts to wane

00:23:38.470 --> 00:23:43.140
I stand under the lazy morning's light

00:23:44.060 --> 00:23:47.440
And when that same moon rises

00:23:47.440 --> 00:23:56.280
I'll start moving all over again

00:24:04.830 --> 00:24:06.890
The Deltora Encyclopedia

00:24:06.890 --> 00:24:07.950
<i>Dread Gnomes.
The Deltora Encyclopedia</i>

00:24:07.950 --> 00:24:08.340
The Deltora Encyclopedia

00:24:09.300 --> 00:24:14.630
<i>A proud tribe that had fought the Shadow Lord in the past, excelling in the use of bows.</i>

00:24:14.630 --> 00:24:19.300
<i>But now, they live in an underground cave system, ruled by a monster called 'Gellick'.</i>

00:24:20.820 --> 00:24:26.200
We somehow managed to escape from the Dread Gnomes' trap, and we now need to go and defeat that monster.

00:24:26.600 --> 00:24:29.210
We must get the emerald embedded in its forehead!

00:24:29.750 --> 00:24:30.900
Alright, let's do this!

00:24:30.900 --> 00:24:31.990
Defeat the Great Gellick

00:24:31.990 --> 00:24:34.690
Next time, 'Defeat the Great Gellick'.

